    "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: Mindustry terrain floor texture atlas, strict vertical top-down orthographic. Create NEW painted GROUND TEXTURES only. Use attached approved mail and party references ONLY for the refined bright clean Daoist Q hand-painted finish and restrained jade/ivory/warm stone material harmony. DO NOT draw UI frames, letters, numbers, labels, characters, symbols, objects, raised blocks or scenery. Terrain retains functional material colors, not all green. Requested 1536×3072 tall image, exactly 3 equal columns × 6 equal rows, EIGHTEEN full-bleed square terrain swatches. NO gaps, gutters, outlines, framing, rounded corners or margins: each 1/3-width by 1/6-height cell is its own continuous FLAT tile. Within every row draw THREE genuinely different variations of its same ground material, with same average color and scale but different cracks/grain/pebble distribution. Do not repeat one tile three times. Texture details only, no elevation view. Each tile should tile on all four edges without dominant cut lines; edges quiet, consistent and natural; broad contrast kept low for gameplay legibility. Soft overhead daylight, high-end delicate hand-painted texture, no photoreal noise.\nRows top to bottom:\n1 STONE: natural pale cool gray limestone with subtle jade-gray shading, rounded embedded stones and fine irregular hairline cracks, mostly smooth walkable ground.\n2 BASALT: darker charcoal blue-gray cooled basalt, small rounded polygon cracks with subdued lighter rims, no lava, retain readable broad shapes.\n3 SHALE: muted purple-gray layered flat shale with irregular overlapping thin flakes embedded in ground, no raised rocky wall.\n4 DIRT: warm cocoa-brown compact earth, occasional tiny embedded pebbles, gentle granular brushwork, no plants.\n5 SAND: warm pale ivory-beige fine desert sand with soft wind ripple brush strokes, no rocks, no dunes viewed from the side.\n6 MUD: damp desaturated warm gray-brown mud, soft smooth wet 